{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/800704-rules-clarification-claws-and-bite-that-grapple-and-pre-empting-an-attack-urhan","id":800704,"title":"Rules clarification: Claws and bite that grapple, and pre-empting an attack (urhan).","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-04T13:16:58-08:00","id":800704,"title":"Rules clarification: Claws and bite that grapple, and pre-empting an attack (urhan).","content":"A wereolf in Gauru form can deal alot of damage with one claw strike. However, it is written in the form section that they can establish a grapple in addition to causing damage. Does that mean lets say that a claw attack mister vampire clown of the suck-brother club, and I deal like 4 damage, he is also considered to be in a grapple if I choose too ? Does that mean that if my attack roll was 5 or more successes, not only do I deal alot of pain, but I also enter grappling with an exceptional success, so I can already deliver a move in the grappling list of move ?<br /> <br /> The there is the Urhan pre-empting things. Since we are starting to play this edition, we are like 4 players and we argument over the correct use of this. Can you explain what pre-empting does, and in like an example, show me exactly how it can be used ?<br /> <br /> Thanks guys. You are awesomes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T13:24:14-08:00","id":800705,"title":"","content":"Yes to everything but getting inflict further damage on the initiating exceptional success.<br /> <br /> So yes, you roll 5 successes and you do the 5 + 2 lethal damage (from a bite anyway), and if you acted before the vampire that turn, he loses his turn and contests the grapple with you next turn. Then you both roll your full Strength + Brawl and whoever wins gets to deliver whatever maneuvers he wishes. Common houserules forbid the Damage maneuver twice.<br /> <br /> The same works with Urhan, though only on a bite. You pre-empt the enemy's turn by spending an essence to attack. Initiate the grapple on attack, same deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T13:31:29-08:00","id":800708,"title":"","content":"Ok, but this is not a double tap. I mean, if Iattack, and I deliver a strike, or a bite... with like 3 successes, I do 5 damage, and I choose to also enter grappling. It does not give me the opportunity to use that grappling move right on the spot. Its just that now, im considered grappling. But if I do roll on my attack 5 or more successes instead of 3. Not only do I deliver alot of damage, but I can also choose a grappling move already, and we both contest it right now, since my turn is not over ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T13:35:14-08:00","id":800709,"title":"","content":"No. You don't get to do a grappling move on that turn because your exceptional success was not on a grapple roll. It was on an attack roll. Your grapple is an auto-effect tagged on the end of your attack, unrelated to whatever successes you rolled. You never get to do a grapple maneuver without some chance at contesting the grapple by your opponent.<br /> <br /> That's my read, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 01-04-2016, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T13:38:16-08:00","id":800712,"title":"","content":"I know that the opponent has a chance of contesting every grapple move you do. I was just thinking that since it was an exceptional success, I was able, in that same turn, to pick a grappling move, and does the contesting roll, me vs the opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T13:40:08-08:00","id":800715,"title":"","content":"Note that werewolf claws do not deal damage to vamps, only bites. This is important to note primarily due to using things like Quicksilver Flesh, which grow claws. <br /> <br /> The general move to establish a Grapple is considered to be a different dice pool than the regular attack from Gauru, Urshul, or Urhan. For instance, certain weapons can be used as an aid in grappling for an equipment modifier equal to weapon rating. The werewolf attack isn't doing that - they're dealing damage, and happen to grapple automatically. So, you're not rolling an exceptional success on a grapple check, you're rolling an exceptional success on an attack roll.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T13:43:09-08:00","id":800718,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the clarification. I do understand perfectly now. I was thinking that it was quite... overkill...<br /> <br /> However, Ihave another request. Using the same vampire, or any other character you like, can you describe an example of a Urhan using his ability to &quot;pre-empt&quot; lets say, an attack. How does that work ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T14:55:31-08:00","id":800756,"title":"","content":"Sure. Vampire's Initiative is 12, Werewolf in Urhan's is 7. Vampire goes first and chooses to attack the werewolf. The Werewolf chooses to spend an essence to attack before the vampire does. Werewolf hits with his attack and chooses to establish a grapple. Vampire loses his turn as he is now grappled, and next turn both will contest the grapple, with the winner being able to enact a maneuver.<br /> <br /> If the werewolf had chosen not to establish a grapple, the vampire would have continued his attack after the werewolf's was completed.<br /> <br /> Next turn Initiatives stay the same as they were, with the vampire attacking first.<br /> <br /> If the vampire used Celerity then re-empt his attack then we run into some complicated stuff that there isn't really guideline for. Perhaps a Clash of Wills or just allow the most recent interrupt to apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 01-04-2016, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T15:07:45-08:00","id":800763,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'm fairly sure that the vampire still has the higher Initiative, so they would contest the grapple during the vamp's turn, which happens immediately after the wolf's action. You do opposed rolls on &quot;each turn... on the higher of the character's Initiatives&quot; not &quot;starting with the next turn.&quot; The pre-emptive attack doesn't change the werewolf's Initiative; he's still got 7, the vamp's still got 12.<br /> <br /> And, yes, if the vamp has Celerity, it turns into Clash of Wills - says it in that very section. The vamp rolls BP + Celerity, the wolf rolls PU + Auspice Renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T16:19:53-08:00","id":800792,"title":"","content":"Fair enough on both counts. Makes sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T19:00:33-08:00","id":800871,"title":"","content":"Note that, accounting for Primal Urge limits on spending Essence, the werewolf (if she has Harmony 7-8, or it's free if she has 4-6) can shapeshift as a reflexive action. Spend Essence to preempt another's action while in Urhan, initiate the grapple, shift to Gauru or Urshul to make resistance much more difficult. It'd be pretty terrifying when the wolf leaps on you and clamps its jaws down on your arm, then suddenly doubles in size. On your next turn, inflict damage and cause Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack, or Knocked Down Tilts, then shift to Gauru to finish off the weakened prey. Or simply shift to Gauru first and just go for the most damage.<br /> <br /> Werewolves on the hunt are terrifying, as you can see. Magnify that by the presence of a whole pack. One or two in Urhan, preempting the prey's actions and slowing it down while snarling Urshul leap upon it to cripple it. Then one or more shift into Gauru to completely eviscerate the prey. Few creatures stand a chance if the wolves are snapping at their heels.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T20:36:55-08:00","id":800946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/800704-rules-clarification-claws-and-bite-that-grapple-and-pre-empting-an-attack-urhan?p=800871#post800871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that, accounting for Primal Urge limits on spending Essence, the werewolf (if she has Harmony 7-8, or it's free if she has 4-6) can shapeshift as a reflexive action. Spend Essence to preempt another's action while in Urhan, initiate the grapple, shift to Gauru or Urshul to make resistance much more difficult. It'd be pretty terrifying when the wolf leaps on you and clamps its jaws down on your arm, then suddenly doubles in size. On your next turn, inflict damage and cause Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack, or Knocked Down Tilts, then shift to Gauru to finish off the weakened prey. Or simply shift to Gauru first and just go for the most damage.<br /> <br /> Werewolves on the hunt are terrifying, as you can see. Magnify that by the presence of a whole pack. One or two in Urhan, preempting the prey's actions and slowing it down while snarling Urshul leap upon it to cripple it. Then one or more shift into Gauru to completely eviscerate the prey. Few creatures stand a chance if the wolves are snapping at their heels.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why the Tactical Shifting Style is my favorite thing ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T00:23:24-08:00","id":801201,"title":"","content":"It's pretty awesome, and it makes fighting <i>one </i>werewolf feel like fighting several. A whole pack fluidly shifting and roaring and leaping amid a battle? That's a frenzied fight I'd love to see but not be a part of. Actually, in the bit of fiction I wrote for the <i>Zibhesi </i>stuff in that thread I tried to capture a bit of that reflexive shifting and stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T04:08:13-08:00","id":801269,"title":"","content":"Tactical Shifting is one of the best FS ever designed. I love it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T04:56:30-08:00","id":801280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/800704-rules-clarification-claws-and-bite-that-grapple-and-pre-empting-an-attack-urhan?p=800715#post800715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that werewolf claws do not deal damage to vamps, only bites. This is important to note primarily due to using things like Quicksilver Flesh, which grow claws.</div> </div> </div> </div>Claws do not do <b>lethal</b> damage to vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/800704-rules-clarification-claws-and-bite-that-grapple-and-pre-empting-an-attack-urhan?p=800712#post800712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that the opponent has a chance of contesting every grapple move you do. I was just thinking that since it was an exceptional success, I was able, in that same turn, to pick a grappling move, and does the contesting roll, me vs the opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not how the contested rolls of grappling work, but that's been clarified later in the thread. 1 contested roll per round of combat, which happens on the initiative/turn of the higher of all the participants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/800704-rules-clarification-claws-and-bite-that-grapple-and-pre-empting-an-attack-urhan?p=800763#post800763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I'm fairly sure that the vampire still has the higher Initiative, so they would contest the grapple during the vamp's turn, which happens immediately after the wolf's action. You do opposed rolls on &quot;each turn... on the higher of the character's Initiatives&quot; not &quot;starting with the next turn.&quot; The pre-emptive attack doesn't change the werewolf's Initiative; he's still got 7, the vamp's still got 12.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/800704-rules-clarification-claws-and-bite-that-grapple-and-pre-empting-an-attack-urhan?p=801269#post801269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tactical Shifting is one of the best FS ever designed. I love it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T18:59:56-08:00","id":801727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/800704-rules-clarification-claws-and-bite-that-grapple-and-pre-empting-an-attack-urhan?p=800871#post800871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that, accounting for Primal Urge limits on spending Essence, the werewolf (if she has Harmony 7-8, or it's free if she has 4-6) can shapeshift as a reflexive action.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always wandered about that. If it is reflexive, meaning unlimited times, can I initiate my turn as Hishu, run as Urhan to chase, bite as Urshul, and be back to Urhan at the end same action? I always treated the answer as YES, but it was always kinda very hard to describe. Probably onlookers only see a blur of fur and teeth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T19:09:26-08:00","id":801729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/800704-rules-clarification-claws-and-bite-that-grapple-and-pre-empting-an-attack-urhan?p=801727#post801727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always wandered about that. If it is reflexive, meaning unlimited times, can I initiate my turn as Hishu, run as Urhan to chase, bite as Urshul, and be back to Urhan at the end same action? I always treated the answer as YES, but it was always kinda very hard to describe. Probably onlookers only see a blur of fur and teeth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Answer is still yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T20:14:23-08:00","id":801747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/800704-rules-clarification-claws-and-bite-that-grapple-and-pre-empting-an-attack-urhan?p=801727#post801727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always wandered about that. If it is reflexive, meaning unlimited times, can I initiate my turn as Hishu, run as Urhan to chase, bite as Urshul, and be back to Urhan at the end same action? I always treated the answer as YES, but it was always kinda very hard to describe. Probably onlookers only see a blur of fur and teeth.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, yes. Rose or Stew or someone could clarify if need be, but the books say reflexive actions can be done at any time and don't take up a combat action. If you can shift reflexively, then presumably you can do it at any time, with a couple exceptions. One is that if you require Essence to do it reflexively, you have to be able to spend that Essence at the chosen time, and the other is that you can only take <i>Gauru </i>once per scene unless you fall into <i>Kuruth</i>, at which point reflexive shapeshifting is not really a concern.<br /> <br /> This is an immensely powerful and versatile ability. In response to a devastating attack you might shift to <i>Urshul </i>for the extra durability\u2014or immediately shift to <i>Gauru </i>for Rage and regeneration. Find yourself chased down by death hounds of a necromancer and see the closed door ahead? Shift to <i>Hishu </i>to open it without breaking it, then shut it and lock it, and if you need to, go back to a faster form to escape further. Or turn <i>Dalu </i>to help force a couch against the door, grab a nearby baseball bat, or await them in <i>Urshul </i>and pounce when they break through the door.<br /> <br /> Essentially, werewolves get access to a lot of free Attribute dots as part of their template, but have to shapeshift to get them. These bonuses come with lots of other nifty abilities like enhanced speed and reflexes, more power, and senses that should be used in every scene. Seriously, as nice as +2 Strength or Dexterity is, do not underestimate the power of senses. Wolves can tell so much by smell, and also hearing, especially powerful in the urban realm where senses are so often dulled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T13:41:13-08:00","id":802315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/800704-rules-clarification-claws-and-bite-that-grapple-and-pre-empting-an-attack-urhan?p=801747#post801747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an immensely powerful and versatile ability. In response to a devastating attack you might shift to <i>Urshul </i>for the extra durability\u2014or immediately shift to <i>Gauru </i>for Rage and regeneration. Find yourself chased down by death hounds of a necromancer and see the closed door ahead? Shift to <i>Hishu </i>to open it without breaking it, then shut it and lock it, and if you need to, go back to a faster form to escape further. Or turn <i>Dalu </i>to help force a couch against the door, grab a nearby baseball bat, or await them in <i>Urshul </i>and pounce when they break through the door.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is, immensely is the right word. However, it opens up some questions regarding fighting styles like Tactical Shifting. For example, let's see Broaden:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF 2e, Page 110</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Broaden (\u2022\u2022): Your character increases quickly in size, forcing nearby opponents to move or be pushed back. When you shift up, anyone within close-combat range who doesn\u2019t Dodge suffers bashing damage equal to the difference in Size between your two forms. Anyone who takes damage must make a Dexterity + Athletics roll or suffer the Knocked Down Tilt (see p. 313).</div> </div> </div> </div>If I have Harmony 4, 5, or 6, what stops me from grappling an opponent and start shifting Up and Down until a kill him? It gets worse with Crush:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF 2e, Page 110</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crush (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): When your character grabs or bites an opponent she can shift up. Her larger form crushes her foe. When your character has another grappled, shifting up reflexively causes automatic lethal damage equal to the difference in Size between her two forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I grab my target and start going back and forth from Hishu and Dalu, killing anything before my turn ends. You can say the same thing from Suck It Up, which let's you reduce incoming damage by one if you shift down. If I can do it reflexively, I'm always reducing damage, not even need to declare it to my storyteller.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would rule that you can only benefit from said maneuver once per turn, but since the whole &quot;infinite shapeshifting&quot; seems a little broken, maybe I will rule that you have ONE free shapeshift per turn, and you may again if you spend Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T14:01:03-08:00","id":802333,"title":"","content":"In that case, I'd just say one maneuver per turn. Multiple actions are gone as is, so allowing a mutant form of extra attacks here would be a big no-no. As far as shapeshifting, your rule is a pretty reasonable one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T14:41:53-08:00","id":802355,"title":"","content":"The wording of Tactical Shifting confuses things a bit, because it specifically permits you to use multiple maneuvers if you shift appropriately (using the example of activating both Springloading and Fluid Movement together). I can't recall if there's a general fighting style rule about each given maneuver only being usable once per turn (unless otherwise specified), but it seems sensible.<br /> <br /> Though using rapid shifting to make yourself into a Were-buzzsaw <b>does </b>seem pretty tactically useful...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T05:10:40-08:00","id":802982,"title":"","content":"My personal ideas on making Tactical Shifting not totally broken are:<br /> You can shift reflexively once per turn.<br /> -or-<br /> You can only benefit from a Maneuver once per round. (which makes sense, with the way Springloading works). You can absorb 1 blow, you can crush once, but this means you can combine Springloading and Suck It Up in 1 round.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}